          "date": "2026-11-11 06:51:22.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: evict failed clients at once in insanity",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: evict failed clients at once in insanity\n\nfail_clients() fails a client with umount -f, which sends no\ndisconnect. The targets keep the client's export and locks\nuntil the ping evictor or a lock callback timeout drops them,\nabout 100 seconds later whatever obd_timeout is, and the live\nclient blocks on those locks in client_rmdirs. An MDT that\nfails over before then also waits for the dead client in\nrecovery, up to the hard limit.\n\nEvict the failed client by UUID on every MDT and OST right\nafter the umount. The tests still fail clients alongside\nserver failures, and a target that is down at the time still\nrecovers without the lost client, as ost1 does in test_6.\nWhat they no longer check is that a target finds the dead\nclient by itself; recovery-small 10d, 26a and 26b do that.\n\nFull insanity, 2 MDTs, 2 OSTs, 2 clients, with obd_timeout 10,\ntwo runs on each tree: 1990 to 624 seconds on average. Tests\n3, 6, 8, 9 and 12 save about 110 seconds each, and 7, 11, 13\nand 14 about 200, since they also skip the 90 second recovery\nof MDT0001. That is about 2,500 hours of CI per 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: testlist=insanity\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=insanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I45b0c73c8fe3c3da26a034bda018fa5d8fbe5c63\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70384\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
